// HZM coop - MULTIPLAYER OPTIONS (host game setup). MP-OWNED menu (coop_mp* name, in MP_MANIFEST), so it may
// name the MP cvars coop_mpMode / coop_mpPreset and the MP armory open cfgs. Pushed from ui/multiplayerstart.urc
// (the Select Game Type screen) via the one coop-file-legal bridge token "coop_mpmenu" (check_mp_isolation clause 7
// special-cases it). Loaded automatically by the engine ui/*.urc sweep (cl_ui.cpp CL_InitializeUI:5690), so no coop
// file registers it. INERT in coop: never pushed there, and its buttons only set coop_mp* cvars when clicked.
//
// WIRING: each mode button does `set coop_mpMode <x>` and each preset button `set coop_mpPreset <x>` (plain set, no
// vstr - clause 18). mp.scr::main reads both with getcvar at MP map load, so the host picks here, then picks a map
// and starts it in the normal DM flow; the cvars are in effect when the MP server spawns. A level load wipes level
// vars, so the mode can never follow anyone into coop.
//
// SELECTED-STATE READOUT: enabledcvar tests integer truthiness only (uiwidget.cpp isEnabled), so it cannot gate a
// tile on a STRING cvar value. Instead a single readout Label per row uses linkcvar + linkstring, which does string
// equality (uilabel.cpp FindLinkString:151) and shows the friendly name of the current pick. Before any click the
// cvar is unregistered, so UI_FindCvar returns NULL and the Label falls back to its title (uilabel.cpp:258).
//
// COOP LOADOUT: the third button ("CHANGE COOP LOADOUT") opens the EXISTING coop loadout screen READ-ONLY via
// `exec ui/loadout/open.cfg` - the same opener coop itself uses (open.cfg seeds view state, pushes coop_loadout,
// pings the name bus, seeds gloves). This is a USER-APPROVED narrow isolation exception (2026-09-14): read-only UI
// navigation to the already-existing coop armory - it changes no coop file (coop_loadout.urc stays checksum-locked),
// calls no coop script, and writes no coop cvar. check_mp_isolation scopes the exception to EXACTLY this one file
// plus the one opener token ui/loadout/open.cfg (CLAUSE12_COOP_OPENER); any other ui/loadout token here still fails
// clause 12, and this file must still never name coop_lo* or the coop_loadout menu directly (it goes through open.cfg).
//
// URC conventions: each resource field on its own line (single-line blocks silently drop); colour fills for panels,
// never raw-image shaders (bug-menu-shader-label-invisible); canvas stays 640x480 (bug-1365); ASCII, no em-dash.
menu "coop_mpmenu" 640 480 NONE 1
borderstyle NONE
bgcolor 0 0 0 0
align centerx centery
virtualres 1
fullscreen 0

direction from_top 0

